    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to exploit several favorable matchups today, with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our strongest play. His score of 83.29 is buoyed by an elite 19% boost from opposing starter Johnson\u2019s weak xERA of 5.15 and a significant platoon advantage that amplifies his power potential. Alongside him, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Andy Pages** (74.01) provide top-tier utility. While **Jackson Merrill** faces a slight efficiency tax due to the opponent's ability to hold runners, his prime #3 spot in the order against the vulnerable Ritchie makes him a cornerstone for our run and RBI production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also remains a locked-in starter, benefiting from a +8% order bump and a favorable matchup against Lambert to sustain a strong 70.08 rating.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s slate involved the final utility spot, where **Nolan Schanuel** (59.93) narrowly edged out **Josh Jung** (54.92) to maintain our efficiency floor. While **Josh Jung** provides reliable production, his matchup against Alcantara\u2014a tougher assignment than the one facing **Nolan Schanuel**\u2014pushed the optimizer to favor the latter\u2019s steady contact profile. We are also keeping a close watch on **Drake Baldwin**, whose 58.63 score is heavily supported by a high xwOBA (0.378) despite a lukewarm matchup against Peralta. Owners should note that the platoon disadvantage facing **Dominic Smith** (46.76) makes him the most volatile piece of our starting lineup; if his official order position drops or conditions shift, he remains our primary candidate for a mid-game swap with **Josh Jung** or **Miguel Vargas** should the need for a pinch-hit replacement arise.",
